{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out","id":1205867,"title":"C20 Book of Freeholds is out!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T19:17:49-07:00","id":1205867,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> C20 Book of Freeholds is out!","content":"Yeah its out but I can't seem to download it or the Map of Concordia right now? Its not letting me, is it cause everyone is downloading right now and breaking it?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:28:13-07:00","id":1205870,"title":"","content":"Ok.. how do Nobles have multiple powerful balefires if they have to spend 1 point of glamour each to attune them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:33:10-07:00","id":1205871,"title":"","content":"I could only get it to work by sending it to my Dropbox first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:37:47-07:00","id":1205874,"title":"","content":"...welp, here's my regret for not getting a tier with Deluxe C20.<br /> <br /> Ah well. I could wait the few extra months...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:09:48-07:00","id":1205883,"title":"","content":"Okay figured it out, it wouldn't let me download any other way but checking the box and clicking the download checked box method.<br /> <br /> Seems odd so Kithain seem to have spread all over the world and are the world's Changelings, except Menehune and Nunnehi have their own pockets of nonkithain changelings, and they clarify Hsien aren't chimerical, and are pretty much like they used to be... We could use some more Kiths from around the World, as well as foreign houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:13:28-07:00","id":1205884,"title":"","content":"Forgot to google something.. ignore this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:21:56-07:00","id":1205889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205883#post1205883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems odd so Kithain seem to have spread all over the world and are the world's Changelings, except Menehune and Nunnehi have their own pockets of nonkithain changelings, and they clarify Hsien aren't chimerical, and are pretty much like they used to be... We could use some more Kiths from around the World, as well as foreign houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugggggghhhhhh.....goddammit.<br /> <br /> Look, I subscribe to the idea of the Dreaming being universal and the archetypes the Kithain represent definitely being found in fairy/folk tales all over the world...but there's a limit. Regional variations should absolutely be a thing: the people's Dreams should be similar, but still wholy unique on their own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:29:23-07:00","id":1205895,"title":"","content":"But here's the thing, the Nunnehi and Menehune are presented as being cut off from their Dreams (and their cultures), and the Hsien are presented as if people in China and Japan and whatnot don't even have Dreams. It's not just weird and discordant, it's disturbingly racist to the point where I get embarrassed presenting Changeling to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:31:07-07:00","id":1205897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205889#post1205889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ugggggghhhhhh.....goddammit.<br /> <br /> Look, I subscribe to the idea of the Dreaming being universal and the archetypes the Kithain represent definitely being found in fairy/folk tales all over the world...but there's a limit. Regional variations should absolutely be a thing: the people's Dreams should be similar, but still wholy unique on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm it does seem though they had foresight to not completely write everyone as familiar kiths. Some kithain are born for instance in Hong Kong, a Satyr and Sidhe who are cousins, and this could be due to the connection to Great Britain. And the Changelings in Uluru in Australia and some Buntu changelings (who are noted for Guarding the Wonder Caves Glade for Millenia and are thus likely to not be of the standard kithain since they are from before the Fae became standardized into the western kiths, are not given kiths, which I take as a blessing because I believe they intentionally did that hoping we could get some regional kiths in the area, while they still mention specific Sidhe Lords in the areas. <br /> <br /> But I don't see talk about the overlap of Changelings and Hsien. The Hsien are said to be changelings, just far removed from the Kithain and closer to the Nunnehi/Menehune, and their dragon's nests are not Chimerical. But with kithain in Tokyo does that mean they had to spread there through connections with the rest of the world?<br /> <br /> A bit inconsistent but I'll take it over not leaving any room for expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:39:22-07:00","id":1205909,"title":"","content":"Haha, Underbridge!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:53:03-07:00","id":1205916,"title":"","content":"Yeah I love the Underbridge, and while I tried to only skim, I pretty much read most of the Example Glades, good stuff. Lots of fun story seeds in this book well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:08:59-07:00","id":1205918,"title":"","content":"Having to imbue each Freehold with a point of glamour seems excessive especially when they suggest personal holdings as a thing..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:16:27-07:00","id":1205920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205918#post1205918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having to imbue each Freehold with a point of glamour seems excessive especially when they suggest personal holdings as a thing..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that was always a thing though... Freeholds are expected to outlast the changeling that created them after all, and there are a butt load of changelings compared to most other supernaturals next to Wraiths, and maybe Fallen. Most other supernaturals have a much harder time creating a place of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:19:28-07:00","id":1205921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205870#post1205870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok.. how do Nobles have multiple powerful balefires if they have to spend 1 point of glamour each to attune them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Freeholds don't have to start with all their Balefires, the one in Spain, the Thorpe had Marisiel only start with two, and an allied commoner created another. So maybe they have help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:25:31-07:00","id":1205924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205920#post1205920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that was always a thing though... Freeholds are expected to outlast the changeling that created them after all, and there are a butt load of changelings compared to most other supernaturals next to Wraiths, and maybe Fallen. Most other supernaturals have a much harder time creating a place of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but as say a mage.. I don't have take a permanent point of Paradox per Node I control. As a buyable background that basically costs you your glamour it seems odd. Not just in that making things are hard but also in that attuning the freehold costs you a point<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205921#post1205921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Freeholds don't have to start with all their Balefires, the one in Spain, the Thorpe had Marisiel only start with two, and an allied commoner created another. So maybe they have help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remembered Chimerical sacrifice was a thing.. that will work well for one of my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:26:27-07:00","id":1205926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205895#post1205895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here's the thing, the Nunnehi and Menehune are presented as being cut off from their Dreams (and their cultures), and the Hsien are presented as if people in China and Japan and whatnot don't even have Dreams. It's not just weird and discordant, it's disturbingly racist to the point where I get embarrassed presenting Changeling to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh boy...I know someday I'll have to take a look into the Asian WoD stuff. But from what I hear, they treat it to the point of making Asia this odd place where the rest of the World of Darkness just doesn't want to interact with because it's so WEIRD and ALIEN and DANGEROUS...and I have no idea why they made it that way.<br /> <br /> And I just get amused how even nu-WW, with ALL of their controversial decisions and statements, even they are hesitant at the idea of doing a theoretical Kindred of the East 5th edition.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to keep up hope that a Book of Gallain (bare minimum: I'm in the camp that would prefer the Nunnehi, Menehune, and Hsien get their own standalone books) arrives to give them the proper write-up and expansions they deserve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205897#post1205897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't see talk about the overlap of Changelings and Hsien. The Hsien are said to be changelings, just far removed from the Kithain and closer to the Nunnehi/Menehune, and their dragon's nests are not Chimerical. But with kithain in Tokyo does that mean they had to spread there through connections with the rest of the world?<br /> <br /> A bit inconsistent but I'll take it over not leaving any room for expansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>...even though the Hsien's method of gaining Glamour is completely different from the Nunnehi's and the Menehune's way...?<br /> <br /> Although with the idea of Kithain in Japan, that I can buy. Japan has had a history of &quot;borrowing&quot; from other cultures and them remaking it in their own way. For example, the entire anime industry was based around admiration in the original Disney cartoons. And some of the Kithain I could see developing into the form of known Japanese yokai. So that's not too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:37:47-07:00","id":1205929,"title":"","content":"Its because Nunnehi and Menehune are attuned to the Umbra, and the Hsien are as well.<br /> <br /> You could interpret things that things like the rise of Monotheism resulted in mythic beings being more often denied, and thus Western Mythic creatures fell into hiding in dreams rather then being ignored, while in many parts of the World Animism or at least pantheism provided a way for mythic beings to not need to tie themselves to the Dreaming. Hence why Dark Age Fae isn't so much a game tied to the Dreaming. So when the Kithain spread some chose to join them, like the Eshu who were in between the animism and gods of Africa and Islam and choose to join the Kithain.<br /> <br /> The original Hsien book was pretty great considering they only had one book to work with. Its more the Middle Kingdom books were unified and ignored the Dreaming entirely. Like the Wan Kuei the Hsien were more a reimagining of the concept of changelings then being restricted by tying into the history of the gameline. So Nunnehi and Hsien didn't have to deal with the Dreaming because they did't suffer from disbelief and thus were allowed to stay in their familiar territories of the Umbra and the Autumn World. Kithain came and brought an influx of dreaming activities with them. Nunnehi/Menehune are more the inbetweeners between the Changelings of the Kithain and their strict tie to the Dreaming, and the Hsien and their blindness to the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:38:33-07:00","id":1205931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205926#post1205926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh boy...I know someday I'll have to take a look into the Asian WoD stuff. But from what I hear, they treat it to the point of making Asia this odd place where the rest of the World of Darkness just doesn't want to interact with because it's so WEIRD and ALIEN and DANGEROUS...and I have no idea why they made it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't have good access to Asian media outside anime and Hong Kong films.. which basically was enough to get the idea that things were kind of different over there?<br /> <br /> I mean africa was just as much &quot;wierd and mysterious&quot; too.<br /> <br /> ON THE OTHER HAND American supernaturals being practically blind to anything outside America and assuming either &quot;Its foreign and awesome&quot; or &quot;its foreign and confusing smash&quot; IS pretty much in keeping with Americans!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I just get amused how even nu-WW, with ALL of their controversial decisions and statements, even they are hesitant at the idea of doing a theoretical Kindred of the East 5th edition. </div> </div> </div>Um they put up a thing for the ST Vault with some signficant updates that show an intent to do SOMETHING with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although with the idea of Kithain in Japan, that I can buy. Japan has had a history of &quot;borrowing&quot; from other cultures and them remaking it in their own way. For example, the entire anime industry was based around admiration in the original Disney cartoons. And some of the Kithain I could see developing into the form of known Japanese yokai. So that's not too bad. </div> </div> </div>I&quot;ll say this once again Pooka are better at being Tanuki than the actually Tanuki splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:41:12-07:00","id":1205933,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair a lot of that can be rectified if you give the Hsien more Powers, meanwhile changelings have a buttload of Changeling Arts that can simulate a ton of different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:43:28-07:00","id":1205936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205933#post1205933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair a lot of that can be rectified if you give the Hsien more Powers, meanwhile changelings have a buttload of Changeling Arts that can simulate a ton of different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hsien.. don't need more powers. They pretty much are the prototype for DA Mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pooka make better Tanuki because they can turn into the Right animal and have a more appropriate sort of trickster attitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:48:41-07:00","id":1205939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205936#post1205936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hsien.. don't need more powers. They pretty much are the prototype for DA Mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pooka make better Tanuki because they can turn into the Right animal and have a more appropriate sort of trickster attitude</div> </div> </div> </div>Well since C20 the Tanuki don't turn into badgers anymore, which was a horrible mistranslation since Raccoon dogs are real animals. But they don't really have illusion or shapeshifting powers like those provided by Arts so they really could use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:51:54-07:00","id":1205954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205939#post1205939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well since C20 the Tanuki don't turn into badgers anymore, which was a horrible mistranslation since Raccoon dogs are real animals. But they don't really have illusion or shapeshifting powers like those provided by Arts so they really could use them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's.. level one of Nei tan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T00:11:57-07:00","id":1205959,"title":"","content":"Doh forgot Neitan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:43:50-07:00","id":1206075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1205926#post1205926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh boy...I know someday I'll have to take a look into the Asian WoD stuff. But from what I hear, they treat it to the point of making Asia this odd place where the rest of the World of Darkness just doesn't want to interact with because it's so WEIRD and ALIEN and DANGEROUS...and I have no idea why they made it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are role-playing games created by mostly White males. If they try to create stories and characters centered around an Asian culture--even if it's treated with respect, they will undoubtedly still get crap from this community(on here, or other forums).<br /> <br /> If they DON'T try to create stories and characters centered around an Asian culture, then they will get crap from this community.<br /> <br /> Sure, they could reach out to Asian people who work in this industry to make it more authentic, but I don't think that's an especially easy thing to do with the state the industry is in right now.<br /> <br /> And I, as someone who purchases their products, would like to see them hire people who are qualified for the position, and not just people who are hired to check off a box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:15:39-07:00","id":1206092,"title":"","content":"<br /> From my understanding there are not many specific peoples of color in the industry because it is such a small and specialized industry, but if you tap into the more general fantasy/fictional writer community you could get qualified folks. But I don't think you need to be asian to write about the culture, Malcom for instance has done a great job and knows quite a lot about the subject particularly Buddhism. Similarly David Hill was pretty good with Asia. It seems though they concentrated only on Hong Kong and Japan. I mean we keep getting multiple Japanese examples in the book, I feel we should have touched upon Taiwan, South Korea and Singapore as well, or the Philippines. All these would have an influx of western Kith without as staunch hegemony from say the Hsien. India and Thailand would have been interesting considering they would have had Hsien not centered on China or Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:28:04-07:00","id":1206100,"title":"","content":"There are a number of non-white people who now write for Onyx Path, and a heck of a lot in roleplaying games as a whole. There are a *lot* of them who live in Asia as well. It's just a matter of willing to go to them for development work instead of asking your buddies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:36:01-07:00","id":1206102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1206100#post1206100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a number of non-white people who now write for Onyx Path, and a heck of a lot in roleplaying games as a whole. There are a *lot* of them who live in Asia as well. It's just a matter of willing to go to them for development work instead of asking your buddies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize that was the case, I know some of the new writers for Scion were, but I didn't realize there were a &quot;lot&quot;. But I'm all for new writers, that is how you broaden the talent pool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T00:12:05-07:00","id":1206311,"title":"","content":"It seems gross that the book is dedicated to Matthew MacFarland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member"