class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1206758#post1206758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything on freeholds in the Pacific Northwest of the United States in the C20 Book of Freeholds?<br /> <br /> Changeling is my second favorite WoD game next to Mage. I missed the Kickstarter and have a Mage 20 game set in Portland, Oregon, so I might be able to use the C20 Book of Freeholds in my game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> [quote book of freeholds]The Emperor Norton Academy near Portland, WA is<br /> Concordia\u2019s premiere educational institute for faerie<br /> lore and Kithain heritage.[/quote]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T19:49:42-07:00","id":1206769,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s much more focused on what freeholds are, their relationship to changeling society, and how to use them in chronicles for players and STs than going in depth into any given freehold. It\u2019s pretty much the opposite of the Freeholds and Hidden Glens Book.<br /> <br /> That said, there\u2019s about a freehold or two per page to illustrate various things the book talks about plus a chapter of sample freeholds. They can mostly be dropped in or adapted for use just about anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T07:45:51-07:00","id":1206879,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the information. I'll look for the Drivethrurpg.com sales announcement in the Monday meeting notes.<br /> <br /> Sample freeholds plus building rules are quite useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:22:53-07:00","id":1206910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1206316#post1206316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably you missed the rape accusations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if anything, I think there should be a... careful approach to Mr. McFarland and his person.<br /> .... firk... I thought we were done with that issue.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Anyways.<br /> <br /> I like the book, but I'm also a bit concerned with the previous statements about the East Asian and Pacific Kithains...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:13:21-07:00","id":1206998,"title":"","content":"The Hsien were set up in Land of Eight Million Dreams. These are anniversary books, so they are what they are. <br /> <br /> In my home games, I treat them more like any other kith. It doesn\u2019t take much effort to do that, so I\u2019d recommend it for folks who, like me, aren\u2019t comfortable with how much Land of Eight Million Dreams others the Asian fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:14:51-07:00","id":1207011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1206998#post1206998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hsien were set up in Land of Eight Million Dreams. These are anniversary books, so they are what they are.<br /> <br /> In my home games, I treat them more like any other kith. It doesn\u2019t take much effort to do that, so I\u2019d recommend it for folks who, like me, aren\u2019t comfortable with how much Land of Eight Million Dreams others the Asian fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have a hard time explaining how they differ from Inanimae and Pooka.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So a question about the book, how does chimerical Resources work? I'm having a hard time figuring how to apply it properly and how people buy what you sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:14:25-07:00","id":1207030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205867-c20-book-of-freeholds-is-out?p=1207011#post1207011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have a hard time explaining how they differ from Inanimae and Pooka.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that house rule, the difference between a pooka and a tanuki would be more like the difference between a pooka and a selkie. I personally don\u2019t like fae having fundamentally different rules just because they\u2019re from a different part of the world. Innanime are the only non-Fomorian Gallain I like having different rules for how they function since they\u2019re born from the dreams of stone, air, fire, water, plants, and certain inanimate objects instead of the dreams of humanity. But again, that\u2019s me personally in my home games. It has nothing to do with what\u2019s in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:32:02-07:00","id":1207056,"title":"","content":"I ended up using the elemental things as the five Chinese Houses (also tied to the five directions and five mystic animal guardians), sort of like the ones from Changeling: The Lost, with a slight variation of the Sidhe being members of the grand celestial bureaucracy and the other Kiths or slight variations being spread around as various folk lore creatures. I've found that Redcaps make a nice baseline template for Same-Bito and Kappa, as well as the demons She Wujing and/or Zhu Bajie from Journey to the West, while Satyrs work as a starting point for Sheng Sheng, and Boggins for most household spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T22:13:14-07:00","id":1207162,"title":"","content":"Australia has sacred sites other than Uluru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T22:16:45-07:00","id":1207163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_contain